{"step_index":395,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T08:15:52Z","input_tokens":2337,"cache_read_tokens":205614,"output_tokens":273,"content":"The graphical prompt timed out because background processes cannot open interactive password prompts. \n\nThe easiest and quickest way to format your pendrive and make it bootable is to **open your terminal** (`Ctrl + Alt + T`) and paste this single command:\n\n```bash\nsudo /home/melwinabi/ventoy/ventoy-1.1.18/Ventoy2Disk.sh -I -g /dev/sda\n```\n\n*(Enter your Ubuntu laptop password when asked).*\n\nThis will format `/dev/sda` into a **GPT UEFI-bootable drive** named **`Ventoy`**. Once Chrome finishes downloading the Windows 11 ISO, simply move the `.iso` file into that **`Ventoy`** USB drive, and your bootable pendrive is ready!"}
